# This repository only ever runs inside a Linux container: the Dockerfile COPYs the whole
# tree into the image. So every text file is checked out with LF on every platform.
# text=auto still lets Git detect binary content, so images/*.png are left alone.
#
# eol=lf is load bearing, not cosmetic. The s6 service scripts under init/ have no file
# extension, so a rule like "*.sh eol=lf" does not reach them. On a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true they come out CRLF, their shebang reads "bashio\r", and s6 cannot exec
# it. The container then starts and reports healthy while the ring-mqtt process never runs,
# looping on "exec: fatal: unable to exec bashio: No such file or directory".
* text=auto eol=lf
